{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfUdnPyo8C5CruaBtBkQa","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I made two small fixes to `0.html`; the file was already in good shape, so I left the rest alone. Neither change has been tested in a browser.\n\n- **`hidden` now works on tables.** The `table { display: block }` rule (and `display: table` in print) overrode the browser's `hidden` styling, so `<table hidden>` would still have displayed. I added a rule that enforces `hidden`, leaving `hidden=\"until-found\"` alone so find-in-page reveal still works.\n- **Open `<details>` has spacing.** The summary sat flush against the content below it when expanded; it now has a 0.5rem gap.\n\nOne thing I left as is: `display: block` on tables can strip table semantics for screen readers in older Safari versions. The robust fix is wrapping tables in a scrollable `<div>`, which means changing markup rather than CSS, so it is only worth doing if you expect real data tables.\n\nThe page content is still just the title and heading \"0\", with no meta description. If \"improve\" meant the content or visual design rather than the base stylesheet, tell me what the page is for and I'll take it from there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3822,"cache_read_input_tokens":7371,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3822},"output_tokens":355,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6c73c8e-93ac-4f4d-b1e0-918a6fa6bdcc","uuid":"47731053-96bb-490e-95bb-e8a0af0d6f72","timestamp":"2026-09-27T21:13:55.259Z","request_id":"req_011CfUdnPYVSyK7vDETfqVoZ"}
